{"id":329,"flavor":[{"games":["Shield","Moon"],"text":"To help make its wings grow, it dissolves quantities of prey in its digestive juices and guzzles them down every day."},{"games":["Sword","X","White 2","Black 2"],"text":"The ultrasonic waves it generates by rubbing its two wings together cause severe headaches."},{"games":["Ultra Moon"],"text":"It vibrates its wings to send out odd sound waves. Trainers who are with it need earplugs."},{"games":["Ultra Sun"],"text":"It vibrates its wings to generate ultrasonic waves, causing its prey to faint. Then it buries the prey alive in the sand to preserve it."},{"games":["Sun"],"text":"Rather than using its underdeveloped wings for flight, it rubs them together, producing ultrasonic waves to attack its enemies."},{"games":["Alpha Sapphire","Sapphire"],"text":"Vibrava’s wings have not yet completed the process of growing. Rather than flying long distances, they are more useful for generating ultrasonic waves by vibrating."},{"games":["Omega Ruby","Ruby"],"text":"To make prey faint, Vibrava generates ultrasonic waves by vigorously making its two wings vibrate. This Pokémon’s ultrasonic waves are so powerful, they can bring on headaches in people."},{"games":["Y","LeafGreen","FireRed"],"text":"It generates ultrasonic waves by violently flapping its wings. After making its prey faint, it melts the prey with acid."},{"games":["White","Black","Platinum","Pearl","Diamond"],"text":"It violently shudders its wings, generating ultrasonic waves to induce headaches in people."},{"games":["SoulSilver","HeartGold"],"text":"It vibrates its wings vigorously, creating ultrasonic waves that cause serious headaches."},{"games":["Emerald"],"text":"It looses ultrasonic waves by rubbing its wings together. Since a VIBRAVA’s wings are still in the process of growing, it can only fly short distances."}],"abilities":[{"name":"Levitate","hidden":false,"description":"By floating in the air, the Pokémon receives full immunity to all Ground-type mo